cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PostHarvestPro: postharvest physiology and technology, quality, shelf life and sensory evaluation in the browser"
abstract: >-
  PostHarvestPro is a self-contained web application for postharvest research and teaching that
  runs entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation. It covers
  quality and maturity indices and CIELAB colour (conversions, ΔE*ab, ΔE94, ΔE00 and colour indices),
  ripeness and damage scales and size grading; deterioration kinetics of zero, first and second
  order with AIC, Arrhenius, Q10 and square-root temperature models, shelf life by attribute limit,
  accelerated shelf-life tests and time to rejection with right censoring (Kaplan–Meier, log-rank,
  Weibull, log-normal and log-logistic models); respiration rate and ethylene in static and
  flow-through systems, climacteric classification, steady-state modified-atmosphere design and
  precooling with its refrigeration load; postharvest losses along the value chain with a Sankey
  diagram, critical points and what-if simulation, and mechanical damage curves with logistic
  dose estimation; sensory discrimination tests with Thurstonian d′, power and sample size,
  hedonic, just-about-right penalty, CATA and descriptive profile analyses with panel performance,
  and Williams serving designs; factorial and repeated-measures analysis of postharvest trials with
  Tukey, LSD and Dunnett comparisons and slope comparison; packaging and cold-storage calculators
  (pallet and container loads, vent area, psychrometrics and vapour-pressure deficit, storage cost
  and product compatibility); and a self-contained HTML report. Every engine was validated against
  independent implementations.
